{
 "id": "01a10747-cc39-7af3-8b39-4ccbac0b0a8e",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (changed Oct 2026, when Finance moved to a new accounting tool): plain comma-separated (`,`) with ISO dates `YYYY-MM-DD`. Previously the old tool required `;` and `DD.MM.YYYY`. UTF-8 without a BOM.",
 "summary": "Monthly export: consumer and format (comma CSV, ISO dates since Oct 2026)"
}
